[ti:Virtute the Cat Explains Her Departure]
[ar:Weakerthans]

[00:08.02] It had something to do with the rain
[00:13.18] Leaching loamy dirt
[00:19.11] And the way the back lane came alive
[00:24.29] Half moon whispered, "Go"
[00:30.80] For a while I heard you
[00:35.48] Missing steps in the street
[00:39.81] And your anger pleading
[00:44.58] In an uncertain key
[00:49.33] Singing the sound that you found for me
[00:55.57] When the winter took the tips of my ears
[01:00.22] Found this noisy home
[01:06.83] Full of pigeons and places to hide
[01:11.51] And when the voices die
[01:17.92] I emerged to watch abandoned machines
[01:22.90] Waiting for their men to return
[01:29.99] I remember the way
[01:33.90] I would wait for you
[01:40.59] To arrive with kibble
[01:44.75] And a box full of beer
[01:49.54] How I'd scratch the empties
[01:54.44] Desperate to hear
[01:58.86] You make the sound that you found for me
[02:11.36] After scrapping with the ferals and the tabby
[02:19.08] Let you brush my matted fur
[02:28.29] How I'd knead into your chest while you were sleeping
[02:37.96] Shallow breathing made me purr
[02:45.66] But I can't remember the sound that you found for me
[02:55.09] I can't remember the sound that you found for me
[03:04.08] I can't remember the sound
[03:10.83] 
